{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474163-gangrel","id":1474163,"title":"Gangrel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-07T22:29:56-08:00","id":1474163,"title":"Gangrel","content":"I am waiting with anticipation for None More Dark Publishing's upcoming sourcebook &quot;Wild Hunt - Gangrel&quot;. What generally draws you into creating a Gangrel character in your VtR chronicles? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","user":"Cabaal","date":". 02-11-2022, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T03:38:57-07:00","id":1507929,"title":"","content":"For me personally it is the urban hunter character, which doesn't have to be bestial like in VtM,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T17:05:09-07:00","id":1507979,"title":"","content":"You might be happy to know that <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/395104/Wild-Hunt-Gangrel\" target=\"_blank\">Wild Hunt</a> is already out.<br /> <br /> While the Daeva and the Ventrue are terrifying for their social powers and the Mehket and Nosferatu are great for unease, I particularly enjoy the Gangrel for cutting to the chase-vampires are powerful, brutal creatures who will eat your face. I actually like using them in positions of leadership and authority because of the effect that has on others, and how it serves as a bloody underline to everyone else's posturing.<br /> <br /> PRotean is also jsut a really fun and versatile toolkit, and as WIld Hunt points out, the Gangrel also have a strong spiritual vibe to them that translates well into Vampires more occult sphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T17:37:09-07:00","id":1507980,"title":"","content":"... well now I'm going to have to figure out what game I'm going to inset of a Gangrel led Circle of Crone theosopy cult... there is no religion higher than truth after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T18:49:31-07:00","id":1507987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474163-gangrel?p=1507980#post1507980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... well now I'm going to have to figure out what game I'm going to inset of a Gangrel led Circle of Crone theosopy cult... there is no religion higher than truth after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Banshee Cruac is a thing to envy and fear.<br /> <br /> A bit of dialogue from a Gangrel Prince of mine:<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you know what the first job of a Prince is? Nope, it's not that, none of what you're thinking. I'm not &quot;in charge,&quot; per se. See, the first job of the Prince is to be able to kill any and every single person in the area-to do it efficiently, contestlessly, swiftly, to rid myself of any and all rivals in as few nights as possible.<br /> <br /> My <i>second</i> job is to help you give me as <i>little</i> incentive as possible to do that. When I ask you to do something, I never do it nicely. Every ask is a death threat. Every attempt to follow it is taking your life in your own hands. Every forgiveness asked for is a plea for a night you gave up. If you want to make it in my city, know there are reasons that I never ask more than I can kill anyone with, and that that's exactly what's happening.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-11-2023, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T11:56:39-07:00","id":1508468,"title":"","content":"I always have a soft spot for the Gangrel and Nosferatu clans in VTR as there no pretensions of what they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-15-2023, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T15:47:59-07:00","id":1508493,"title":"","content":"My introduction to the Gangrel came through VtM and that's still more what type of Gangrel I think of when I think of the clan and honestly neither are really my favorites, I'm not a general fan of animalism or fortitude / resilience, I know they can be useful and powerful but they aren't what I enjoy, especially together.<br /> <br /> I don't know the Requiem bloodlines descended from Gangrel very well but in VtM there are 2 Gangrel offshoots I really enjoy. The first is the city Gangrel who combine the Gangrel's protean with celerity and obfuscate. The other is the all female Ahrimane bloodline who posses more of a spiritual side with Spiritus, Animalism and Presence (originally).\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T20:54:48-07:00","id":1508707,"title":"","content":"The most frightening thing about the Gangrel is in truth the most innocuous: they are free in a way other vampires simply aren\u2019t- at least not without a considerable amount of preparation needed. A Gangrel can go anywhere with nothing more than the clothes of their backs and a desire to travel.. and if they have a reason to go somewhere? Like say.. chasing down some punk who offended their sensibilities? That poor son of a bitch will never truly be safe. Other vampires can do the same, sure, but it will potentially take them longer to reach you. With the Gangrel.. your opportunities for a head start are considerably lessened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T07:38:14-07:00","id":1508748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474163-gangrel?p=1508493#post1508493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My introduction to the Gangrel came through VtM and that's still more what type of Gangrel I think of when I think of the clan and honestly neither are really my favorites, I'm not a general fan of animalism or fortitude / resilience, I know they can be useful and powerful but they aren't what I enjoy, especially together.<br /> <br /> I don't know the Requiem bloodlines descended from Gangrel very well but in VtM there are 2 Gangrel offshoots I really enjoy. The first is the city Gangrel who combine the Gangrel's protean with celerity and obfuscate. The other is the all female Ahrimane bloodline who posses more of a spiritual side with Spiritus, Animalism and Presence (originally).\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Masquerade and Requiem Gangrel actually cover different archetypes, with them actually absorbing parts of the Brujah (the rest of that Clan went to the Daeva and Carthians). Gangrel actually drop most of the animal associations in favour of being savage predators with a passion second only to the Daeva. Pretty much all of the Requiem Clans actually combine elements of several Masquerade Clans, as part of returning to broad archetypes.<br /> <br /> As to Bloodlines Requiem just handles them differently. Besides the fact that most are going to be local phenomena there's a wide range of them covering very specific niches, and you should be able to find or make one that adds your preferred Discipline without fuss (or even swaps one out, so Animalism/Celerity/Majesty/Protean is a possibility). Especially as you can now start your Requiem as a member. You can even have Cool Unique Powerz from your Bloodline, if you really want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T09:05:08-07:00","id":1508757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474163-gangrel?p=1508748#post1508748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Masquerade and Requiem Gangrel actually cover different archetypes, with them actually absorbing parts of the Brujah (the rest of that Clan went to the Daeva and Carthians). Gangrel actually drop most of the animal associations in favour of being savage predators with a passion second only to the Daeva. Pretty much all of the Requiem Clans actually combine elements of several Masquerade Clans, as part of returning to broad archetypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware there are differences, that's why I didn't talk about them turning animalistic with frenzies and instead focused on their discipline spread as something I dislike. The disciplines, specifically animalism and resilience maintain the same themes that I dislike. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T09:45:50-07:00","id":1508762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474163-gangrel?p=1508757#post1508757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm aware there are differences, that's why I didn't talk about them turning animalistic with frenzies and instead focused on their discipline spread as something I dislike. The disciplines, specifically animalism and resilience maintain the same themes that I dislike.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, those are the pair they share with the Ventrue &amp; Julii (in Requiem) and Ravnos &amp; Akunanse (in Masquerade).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T10:05:51-07:00","id":1508763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474163-gangrel?p=1508757#post1508757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm aware there are differences, that's why I didn't talk about them turning animalistic with frenzies and instead focused on their discipline spread as something I dislike. The disciplines, specifically animalism and resilience maintain the same themes that I dislike.</div> </div> </div> </div>Discipline Spreads are only half the Clan, at best. Looking at them and ignoring Clan Banes or culture, for either Vampire line, is doing them a disservice.<br /> <br /> That Bane really does impact the Clan, whether that's 1e encouraging them to be dumb muscle or 2e giving them the Brujah's temper. Plus with Requiem making the five common disciplines easy to learn (whereas in Masquerade it was just the three Physicals) it's not hard for even a standard Gangrel to develop good Obfuscate, Celerity, or Vigor. But the reasoning behind their discipline spread feels pretty clear, their specialty is Protean, their first common is Animalism to tie into the idea of being kin to beasts, and for the third Celerity overlaps slightly with Protean's mobility enhancements, Vigor overlaps with it's offensive enhancements (particularly the iconic claws), and Obfuscate fits two other Clans better.<br /> <br /> The Discipline spreads in Requiem are not perfect, notably the Ventrue share the exact two Disciplines you dislike with the Gangrel. Some people even suggest shifting the Disciplines around to give the Nosferatu's Vigor to either the Gangrel or Ventrue.<br /> <br /> That said, I agree that the two Disciplines are not the coolest in the box. Animalism is probably the hardest to use effectively, although it does have some sledgehammer potential, whereas Resilience suffers the uncool fate of being an entirely defensive power. It doesn't mean they can't lead to cool and awesome characters or moments, Nosferatu won't be the smoldering corpse running out of an inferno to claw somebody's face off, but they don't immediately bring them to mind. Particularly as Resilience doesn't stop you from getting all the cosmetic effects of the damage you ignored.<br /> <br /> That said, Requiem does have something like seven lost and minor Clans, several of which gain access to Protean. Notably the Amari have Obfuscate/Protean/Resilience and, while presented as antagonists, would almost certainly work as PCs (especially as most Vitae expenditure isn't the one they get a hefty discount on). Perfect if you want to learn more into the ambush predator idea, and their Bane isn't the worst in the world (especially now that fire isn't so common).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T06:32:07-07:00","id":1508879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474163-gangrel?p=1508763#post1508763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Discipline Spreads are only half the Clan, at best. Looking at them and ignoring Clan Banes or culture, for either Vampire line, is doing them a disservice.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point if I wanted to talk about the clan as a whole. I specifically chose to focus on the disciplines because those are similar across the game lines and because, frankly, they could have the bane of being superman and I still wouldn't enjoy playing one if their disciplines were animalism and fortitude. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Discipline spreads in Requiem are not perfect, notably the Ventrue share the exact two Disciplines you dislike with the Gangrel. Some people even suggest shifting the Disciplines around to give the Nosferatu's Vigor to either the Gangrel or Ventrue. </div> </div> </div>I to have seen that reddit thread. They were incorrect, vigor suits the nosferatu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, Requiem does have something like seven lost and minor Clans, several of which gain access to Protean. Notably the Amari have Obfuscate/Protean/Resilience and, while presented as antagonists, would almost certainly work as PCs (especially as most Vitae expenditure isn't the one they get a hefty discount on). Perfect if you want to learn more into the ambush predator idea, and their Bane isn't the worst in the world (especially now that fire isn't so common). </div> </div> </div>That's straying from the point of the thread a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T09:50:06-07:00","id":1509205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cabaal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474163-gangrel#post1474163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am waiting with anticipation for None More Dark Publishing's upcoming sourcebook &quot;Wild Hunt - Gangrel&quot;. What generally draws you into creating a Gangrel character in your VtR chronicles?</div> </div> </div> </div>There practical wisdom of knowing what they are and not deluding themselves as things they are not and not to mention they are the clan best suited for travelling long distances without a need for serious preperation like the other clans including the Nosferatu and there discipline spread reflects that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T23:53:22-07:00","id":1509259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474163-gangrel?p=1508879#post1508879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a fair point if I wanted to talk about the clan as a whole. I specifically chose to focus on the disciplines because those are similar across the game lines and because, frankly, they could have the bane of being superman and I still wouldn't enjoy playing one if their disciplines were animalism and fortitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well good news! They also have a third Discipline, and beyond two dots you're not required to invest into any of them. Although Resilience is really good, it's actually cool and not the underwhelming Fortitude of Masquerade.<br /> <br /> You also can't talk about their Disciplines without talking about the rest of the Gangrel, it's not like Discipline spreads exist in a vacuum. If the Gangrel had Celerity and Obfuscate they'd be an entirely different archetype (ambush hit and run predators like the Mehket).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I to have seen that reddit thread. They were incorrect, vigor suits the nosferatu. </div> </div> </div>I meant on this forum. I agree that Vigor suits the Haunts, and the fact that the Gangrel and Ventrue are so close fits the lore of the Ventrue being successors to the Julii and makes the two Clans feel related. I also like the Julii dropping Animalism for Vigor, it suddenly turns the Ventrue into the potential hybrid of two Clans created to escape the Julii's pact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's straying from the point of the thread a bit. </div> </div> </div>Hey, you're the one who brought up non-Gangrel Clans as alternatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T06:29:16-07:00","id":1509271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474163-gangrel?p=1509259#post1509259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well good news! They also have a third Disciplines,</div> </div> </div> </div>Better news, I can play a clan I like and get multiple disciplines I like. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and beyond two dots you're not required to invest into any of them. </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware I was required to invest any dots into disciplines I didn't like. What will happen if I don't?<br /> <br /> Edit: I misunderstood your point here, I get what you were saying now. I think it's a bad point but at least now I get it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although Resilience is really good, it's actually cool and not the underwhelming Fortitude of Masquerade. </div> </div> </div>Agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You also can't talk about their Disciplines without talking about the rest of the Gangrel, </div> </div> </div>I can talk about whatever I want, free country and all that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it's not like Discipline spreads exist in a vacuum. If the Gangrel had Celerity and Obfuscate they'd be an entirely different archetype (ambush hit and run predators like the Mehket). </div> </div> </div>It's a feature, not a flaw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hey, you're the one who brought up non-Gangrel Clans as alternatives. </div> </div> </div>I did? Where? Please quote me. Otherwise please don't accuse me of saying things I never said, it's rude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}